# Copy to .env.local and adjust as needed. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# Server-side target for Server Components and the same-origin /api proxy.
# Defaults to http://localhost:8080 when unset.
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Optional Google maps: itinerary maps, the location picker map and road routes.
# Unset or rejected keys fall back to the built-in maps. Browser key: restrict HTTP
# referrers and allow only Maps JavaScript API + Routes API. Rebuild after setting.
# See docs/google-maps-setup.md.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Canonical public URL used for metadata, sitemap and social previews.
# SITE_URL=https://travel-globe.example.com

# Optional: expose a separate API URL directly to browsers instead of using the proxy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com

# Optional comma-separated hostnames/IPs in addition to auto-detected LAN IPv4 addresses.
# NEXT_ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=travel-globe.local

# Recommended Korean map/place search provider. This key is delivered to the browser,
# so restrict its allowed origins to the production and preview frontend domains.
# When omitted or unavailable, the writer falls back to submitted Nominatim searches
# and OpenStreetMap tiles.
# MAPTILER_API_KEY=

# Optional shared counters for the sign-in rate limit. Without them each serverless
# instance counts on its own. The Vercel Upstash integration sets KV_REST_API_URL and
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN, which are read as well.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<db>.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Optional error service. Browser and server errors are always written to the server log;
# with a Sentry DSN they are also sent to that Sentry project (server-side, no SDK).
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>

# Optional photo storage. Create an R2 bucket, API token and public custom domain.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=travel-globe-photos
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://images.example.com
